<title>USA: CalTech, NextWave in deal.</title>
<headline>CalTech, NextWave in deal.</headline>
<dateline>WALNUT CREEK, Calif 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>CalTech International Telecom Corp has agreed to purchase one billion minutes of Personal Communications Service (PCS) airtime on NextWave's all-digital, nationwide PCS network.</p>
<p>CalTech is a competitive local exchange carrier (CLEC) and long distance service reseller operating in California, Illinois, Colorado, and Arizona. CalTech plans to bundle PCS with its wireline offerings for business and residential customers.</p>
<p>NextWave Inc owns a wireless franchise in the U.S. and is currently building an all-digital nationwide PCS network.</p>
</text>
